cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these programs or this check, please cite them as below, together with Stein and Wuthrich, Algorithms for the arithmetic of elliptic curves using Iwasawa theory, Math. Comp. 82 (2013)."
type: software
title: "Sha(389a1)[p^oo] = 0 for every prime p < 14,633"
abstract: "For the rank-2 elliptic curve 389a1, Sha(E/Q)[p^oo] = 0 at the supersingular primes p = 107, 599, 1049, 2957, 6661, 8263, 9397, 9551 (Stein-Wuthrich's Algorithm 11.1 with Pollack's +/- p-adic L-functions computed from Mazur-Tate elements) and at the split multiplicative prime 389 (exceptional zero, L-invariant, Schneider's height); with Stein-Wuthrich's Theorem 12.3 this covers every prime p < 14,633. Two independently written programs, controls and red controls. A computational verification; it does not show that Sha is finite. Not yet peer reviewed."
authors:
